  "context_pill": "Marginal Relief for Domestic Companies",
  "example_summary": "Calculating the statutory tax ceiling and marginal relief for Y Ltd. when total income slightly exceeds the ₹ 10 crore threshold.",
  "source_provision": "### Statutory Tax Matrix for Domestic Companies\n\n| Total Income Threshold | Gross Receipts in P.Y. 2023-24 ≤ ₹ 400 Cr | Gross Receipts in P.Y. 2023-24 > ₹ 400 Cr | Surcharge Rate |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Up to ₹ 1 Crore** | 25% | 30% | **Nil** |\n| **> ₹ 1 Crore up to ₹ 10 Crore** | 25% + 7% Surcharge | 30% + 7% Surcharge | **7%** |\n| **Exceeding ₹ 10 Crore** | 25% + 12% Surcharge | 30% + 12% Surcharge | **12%** |\n\n\n#### Key Statutory Conditions & Thresholds\n\n* **Turnover Benchmark Test:** The basic tax rate of 25% applies only if gross receipts in the specified prior Financial Year (P.Y. 2023-24 for A.Y. 2026-27) do not exceed ₹ 400 Crore; otherwise, the standard rate of 30% applies (assuming special regimes u/s 115BAA / 115BAB are not opted).\n\n* **Marginal Relief Statutory Ceiling:** Where Total Income exceeds ₹ 1 Crore or ₹ 10 Crore, the total tax payable (including surcharge) shall not exceed:  \n  $$\\text{Tax on Threshold Limit (incl. lower Surcharge)} + (\\text{Total Income} - \\text{Threshold Limit})$$\n\n* **Cess Order of Computation:** Health and Education Cess of 4% is levied on the net tax amount derived **after** subtracting the statutory Marginal Relief.\n\n\n> [!IMPORTANT] Statutory Ceiling Rule for Marginal Relief\n> Marginal Relief = Tax Payable on Total Income (incl. Surcharge) − [Tax Payable on Threshold Limit + (Total Income − Threshold Limit)]. Always compute surcharge adjustment prior to levying 4% Health & Education Cess.",
